          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 Writing · Topic 3 · Q15",
          "passageTitle": "Transitions — Q15",
          "passage": "For several centuries after the birth of opera in sixteenth-century Florence, Italian remained the default language in which most opera scores were written. ______ opera singers today, such as the mezzo-soprano J'Nai Bridges, encounter a wide range of Italian terms–from con amore (with love) to moderato (at a moderate tempo)–when following many eighteenth-century opera scores.",
