          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 Writing · Topic 3 · Q23",
          "passageTitle": "Transitions — Q23",
          "passage": "Many English adjectives share a linguistic origin with their associated nouns, like the adjective \"monetary\" and the noun \"money,\" both of which come from the Latin \"monetarius.\" ______ some adjectives do not share an origin with their associated nouns. For example, the adjective \"arboreal\" ultimately comes from the Latin \"arbor,\" while its associated noun, \"tree,\" comes from the Old English \"treow.\"",
