          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 Writing · Topic 3 · Q29",
          "passageTitle": "Transitions — Q29",
          "passage": "Just as the state of Hawaii has a designated state flower, tree, and bird, it also has a state soil: Hilo soil. Hilo is a fitting choice for state soil, in large part because it can be found in abundance across the state. ______ it plays an important role in Hawaii's agricultural industry and is used to grow a variety of crops, like ginger and taro.",
