          "source": "SAToplam 2.0 Writing · Topic 3 · Q32",
          "passageTitle": "Transitions — Q32",
          "passage": "In his essay \"Of Friendship,\" French philosopher Michel de Montaigne explores a relatively light subject, but he addresses heavier fare in \"Of the Uncertainty of Our Judgment.\" Regardless of subject matter, Montaigne works to question his own perspective throughout his essays. ______ his personal motto was \"What do I know?\"",
